WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.590 --> 00:00:06.270
One of the craziest Game of Thrones fan theories claims that Daario Naharis and Euron Greyjoy

00:00:06.270 --> 00:00:10.550
are the same person. And it’s actually kind of possible.

00:00:10.550 --> 00:00:15.389
In A Storm of Swords, Daario Naharis is one
of three captains of the Stormcrows, a mercenary

00:00:15.389 --> 00:00:20.449
company hired by Yunkai to defend the city
from Daenerys Targaryen. Daario kills the

00:00:20.449 --> 00:00:24.359
two other captains and brings the company
to Dany’s side, helping to take Yunkai,

00:00:24.359 --> 00:00:30.550
then Meereen. Daario is a great fighter, and a great talker, arrogant, swaggering and

00:00:30.550 --> 00:00:35.829
ruthless. He wears colourful Tyroshi clothes with a pointed blue beard, though HBO’s

00:00:35.829 --> 00:00:40.370
Daarios look nothing like this. In any case,
Dany falls for him, and the two become lovers,

00:00:40.370 --> 00:00:45.649
in a relationship that represents the temptation
of violence and vengeance – of "fire and

00:00:45.649 --> 00:00:50.520
blood”. Daario’s always offering to kill
people for Dany, like Jorah, and Hizdahr

00:00:50.520 --> 00:00:55.649
zo Loraq, and the Great Masters. He suggests loosing her dragons on her enemies, and doing

00:00:55.649 --> 00:01:01.010
what she likes, without care for responsibility, or who might get hurt. Dany’s horrified

00:01:01.010 --> 00:01:06.859
by his careless brutality, calls him a monster,
but deep down, thinks she’s a monster too.

00:01:06.859 --> 00:01:11.270
Daario is the devil on Dany’s shoulder,
representing her darker side , so he’s central

00:01:11.270 --> 00:01:15.969
to Dany’s internal conflict in A Dance with
Dragons. Throughout this book, while Dany

00:01:15.969 --> 00:01:21.670
stays to rule Meereen, Daario is sent off
on various missions. But at the end of Dance,

00:01:21.670 --> 00:01:26.249
and the start of The Winds of Winter, Daario
is a hostage of the Yunkai’i, while battle

00:01:26.249 --> 00:01:33.249
begins between Dany’s forces, Yunkish forces,
and some unexpected visitors – the ironborn.

00:01:34.009 --> 00:01:39.490
Euron Greyjoy is brother to Balon, Victarion
and Aeron, and an uncle to Asha and Theon.

00:01:39.490 --> 00:01:45.409
He’s a wild, scheming, dangerous man, a
warrior and a manipulator, widely described

00:01:45.409 --> 00:01:50.799
as mad. After being exiled from the Iron
Islands for raping or seducing Victarion’s

00:01:50.799 --> 00:01:55.819
third wife, he spent several years killing
and pillaging across Essos in his ship of

00:01:55.819 --> 00:02:01.079
mutes called the Silence. He claims to have been everywhere from Asshai to the ruins of

00:02:01.079 --> 00:02:06.279
Valyria, and has knowledge of magic and dragons, apparently having captured Pyat Pree and his

00:02:06.279 --> 00:02:11.650
warlock buddies. In a Feast for Crows, Euron returns to the Iron Islands the day after

00:02:11.650 --> 00:02:15.730
big brother Balon’s sudden death, and is
elected king of the Islands on the promise

00:02:15.730 --> 00:02:21.069
that he will conquer Westeros for the ironborn.
After taking the Shields, he sends Victarion

00:02:21.069 --> 00:02:26.290
and the Iron Fleet off to find Daenerys, so
Euron can marry her and capture her dragons

00:02:26.290 --> 00:02:31.349
with the magic horn Dragonbinder. We’re
led to believe that meanwhile, Euron is raiding

00:02:31.349 --> 00:02:35.180
the Reach, but there’s good not to believe that's true. 'Cause Euron’s

00:02:35.180 --> 00:02:39.200
not that interested in the Reach – he says
“[he’d] bring [the ironborn] dragons,

00:02:39.200 --> 00:02:44.629
and they shout out for grapes” – grapes
as in the Reach. So his talk of taking the Reach,

00:02:44.629 --> 00:02:49.599
even of conquering Westeros, might be empty
words to win the ironborn. But even if Euron

00:02:49.599 --> 00:02:54.349
does intend to conquer, he clearly plans to
do it with dragons. So why would he attack

00:02:54.349 --> 00:02:59.689
the Reach and risk the wrath of the Redwyne
fleet before he has dragons? There is some

00:02:59.689 --> 00:03:04.799
raiding going on along the Mander, but there’s no clear evidence that Euron’s a part of it. It’s

00:03:04.799 --> 00:03:09.609
more likely that he’s focussing on his primary
goal – Dany and her dragons. Which we’re

00:03:09.609 --> 00:03:14.719
led to believe Euron leaves in the hands of
Victarion – Victarion, who is “dumb as

00:03:14.719 --> 00:03:19.859
a stump”, is only good at fighting, knows
nothing about magic or dragons, hates Euron

00:03:19.859 --> 00:03:24.840
and plans to take Dany and her dragons for
himself. Why would Euron trust Victarion

00:03:24.840 --> 00:03:30.529
with this job? Here’s what might be going
on – Euron follows the Iron Fleet to Meereen

00:03:30.529 --> 00:03:36.219
– or gets there first, in disguise, perhaps
– he lets Victarion deal with the Yunkai’i,

00:03:36.219 --> 00:03:41.019
lets Victarion’s men blow the deadly horn,
which apparently kills whoever uses it , then

00:03:41.019 --> 00:03:45.879
Euron can reveal himself and take Dany and her dragons. 'Cause Dragonbinder brings

00:03:45.879 --> 00:03:51.310
dragons not to whoever blows the horn, but
to the horn’s master. Euron found the horn,

00:03:51.310 --> 00:03:56.989
and is manipulating Victarion, surely making Euron the horn’s master. So when Dragonbinder

00:03:56.989 --> 00:04:02.680
sounds, dragons will come to the Crow’s
Eye – not in the Reach, but in Slaver’s Bay.

00:04:02.680 --> 00:04:06.980
Using Victarion like this is exactly
the sort of deception and manipulation that

00:04:06.980 --> 00:04:10.889
we should expect from the Crow’s Eye, and
having him turn up at Meereen would be a pretty

00:04:10.889 --> 00:04:15.730
awesome dramatic reveal.
So onto the theory – what evidence is there

00:04:15.730 --> 00:04:20.699
that Daario and Euron are the same person?
For starters, they look pretty similar. They’re

00:04:20.699 --> 00:04:25.539
both attractive, they both have smooth, pale skin, they both have beards – Daario a

00:04:25.539 --> 00:04:30.340
dyed blue beard, and we’ve already seen
dyed blue beards used as disguises. They both

00:04:30.340 --> 00:04:36.069
have blue eyes, though Euron is said to have a “black eye” beneath his patch. Euron

00:04:36.069 --> 00:04:42.419
also has blue lips from drinking shade-of-the-evening,
which could wear off, or be hidden, maybe?

00:04:42.419 --> 00:04:49.419
And Daario has a gold tooth, which could possibly be fake? Overall, they look quite similar.

00:04:49.430 --> 00:04:54.759
Daario and Euron also have very similar skills and personalities. They’re both good talkers,

00:04:54.759 --> 00:04:59.789
good at convincing people. Euron talks his
way onto the Seastone Chair, and Daario talks

00:04:59.789 --> 00:05:04.120
his way into Dany’s bed – both of which are cases of an outsider getting into a place

00:05:04.120 --> 00:05:09.449
they don’t really belong through flattery, the giving of gifts, and overwhelming confidence.

00:05:09.449 --> 00:05:13.699
They both have a talent for mocking and belittling people. They’re both endlessly bragging

00:05:13.699 --> 00:05:18.400
in fanciful, self-aggrandising monologues,
like, Daario says he “would tell you the

00:05:18.400 --> 00:05:23.060
names of all the men [he has] slain, but before [he] could finish … winter would come and

00:05:23.060 --> 00:05:28.319
go and come again”. Euron says he’s “never known defeat … has never bent his knee … has

00:05:28.319 --> 00:05:33.720
sailed to Asshai by the Shadow, and seen wonders and terrors beyond imagining”. But beneath

00:05:33.720 --> 00:05:39.099
the bravado, both men are dangerous, brutal, men without conscience, who kill like it

00:05:39.099 --> 00:05:43.660
means nothing. They both have a tendency to anger. And they seem to share an interest

00:05:43.660 --> 00:05:48.220
in dragons – Euron’s endlessly talking
about them, and plans to steal Dany’s, while

00:05:48.220 --> 00:05:53.229
Daario brings up dragons many times for someone
who only appears in a few chapters. There

00:05:53.229 --> 00:05:59.009
are weird connections in the show, too. In
Season 3, Daario says he refuses to pay prostitutes,

00:05:59.009 --> 00:06:04.300
which is refusing to pay the gold price, which is an ironborn thing. Also, at one point

00:06:04.300 --> 00:06:10.259
Daario describes a flower, his gift to Dany,
as “beautiful but poisonous” – and we know

00:06:10.259 --> 00:06:16.199
that “Euron’s gifts are poisoned”. But
thirdly, and most maddeningly, in the show,

00:06:16.199 --> 00:06:20.870
Daario captures the ships of the Meereenese
navy. “How many ships?” you might ask.

00:06:20.870 --> 00:06:26.110
“Ninety-three, your Grace” . Ninety-three
ships. That is the same number of ships as

00:06:26.110 --> 00:06:31.849
Victarion leaves with to go to Meereen in
the books. This is not a coincidence, right?

00:06:31.849 --> 00:06:35.289
Either the writers of the show are fucking
with us, or the fleet of ships that Daario

00:06:35.289 --> 00:06:39.740
gives Dany in the show are somehow equivalent
to the fleet of ships Euron sends to Dany

00:06:39.740 --> 00:06:43.430
in the books. There are a bunch of different
ways that could work but either way, it's

00:06:43.430 --> 00:06:48.479
a strong connection between Daario and Euron.
And there’s more – Daario wears Tyroshi

00:06:48.479 --> 00:06:53.720
clothes, and skilfully wields a Dothraki arakh and a Myrish stiletto, which suggests he’s

00:06:53.720 --> 00:06:58.090
pretty well-travelled. We know Euron’s been
all over the world. And Daario has “a gift

00:06:58.090 --> 00:07:02.099
for sleeping”, he’s able to sleep on horseback during storms, which is the sort of skill

00:07:02.099 --> 00:07:06.379
you’d learn spending years at sea. Daario
rhetorically asks if he “Would … steal

00:07:06.379 --> 00:07:11.500
from [Dany]” when Euron’s plan is to steal
dragons from Dany. And Daario and Euron both

00:07:11.500 --> 00:07:16.770
have lines describing men as meat. There
are also symbolic connections, like, Daario’s

00:07:16.770 --> 00:07:21.539
mercenary company is called the Stormcrows,
when Euron is repeatedly described as “the

00:07:21.539 --> 00:07:25.960
storm”, and his nickname is “Crow’s
Eye”. The show changed Daario’s company

00:07:25.960 --> 00:07:31.199
to the Second Sons, but for what it’s worth
Euron is literally a second son. So Daario

00:07:31.199 --> 00:07:36.259
and Euron are similar in appearance and personality
and there are lots little hints at a connection

00:07:36.259 --> 00:07:40.400
between the two. Nothing that proves they’re
the same person, but enough to suggest

00:07:40.400 --> 00:07:46.069
that there might be something here.
So does it make sense for Daario to be a false

00:07:46.069 --> 00:07:52.319
identity of Euron? What does Euron get by
pretending to be some random sellsword? Well,

00:07:52.319 --> 00:07:57.729
we know Euron wants to marry Dany and take
her dragons. By playing the role of Daario,

00:07:57.729 --> 00:08:01.819
Euron has won Dany’s love – she wants
to marry him, says she’d give up her crown

00:08:01.819 --> 00:08:07.139
for him. This explains why Euron is so confident that Dany will marry him, which is ridiculous

00:08:07.139 --> 00:08:12.250
otherwise. Being Daario also allows Euron
to get an insider’s view of the situation

00:08:12.250 --> 00:08:16.080
in Meereen, and what the deal is with the
dragons, which would all be very valuable

00:08:16.080 --> 00:08:21.289
information to someone planning to make a
move there. Being Daario also works with Euron

00:08:21.289 --> 00:08:26.210
secretly being in Slaver’s Bay – as Daario,
he’s a hostage of the Yunkai’i. So he

00:08:26.210 --> 00:08:30.759
just sits tight and waits for Victarion to
use Dragonbinder, bringing a dragon to break

00:08:30.759 --> 00:08:35.640
Euron out of Yunkish custody, so he can hop
on the dragon, maybe kill Victarion while

00:08:35.640 --> 00:08:40.300
he waits for Dany to return to Meereen on
Drogon, so Euron can be all like ‘Heyy,

00:08:40.300 --> 00:08:45.360
it’s’a me, Daario, your dragon seems to
like me for some reason, wanna go spread some

00:08:45.360 --> 00:08:50.190
fire and blood up in these slavers?’ Admittedly, assuming a false identity on the other side

00:08:50.190 --> 00:08:54.130
of the world might not be the best way to
achieve all this. But it could make some kind

00:08:54.130 --> 00:09:00.910
of sense to a mind like Euron’s. Maybe.
Does Daario=Euron fit with what we know of

00:09:00.910 --> 00:09:06.750
Daario? Well, we don’t know much about Daario. In the show he says he’s the son of a prostitute,

00:09:06.750 --> 00:09:12.950
and as far as we know he has no family,
no friends, no gods. What we do know is that

00:09:12.950 --> 00:09:17.870
he’s treacherous. Daario first came to Dany
by breaking contract with Yunkai and killing

00:09:17.870 --> 00:09:23.170
his colleagues. Jorah warns Dany that Daario
is not “worthy of trust”, that “Even

00:09:23.170 --> 00:09:28.570
his beard wears false colors”. Dany rejects
this, saying Jorah’s just jealously pushing

00:09:28.570 --> 00:09:32.920
men away from her, which is probably partly true. But, in arguing that Jorah’s warnings

00:09:32.920 --> 00:09:38.070
are wrong, she lists them: “Pyat Pree’s
a liar, Xaro’s a schemer, Belwas a braggart,

00:09:38.070 --> 00:09:44.240
Arstan an assassin”. Thing is – Pyat Pree
is a liar, Xaro is a schemer, Belwas is a

00:09:44.240 --> 00:09:49.830
braggart, and while Barristan’s not an assassin,
he does deceive Dany. As Dany later admits,

00:09:49.830 --> 00:09:54.370
“[Jorah] always [gives] good counsel”. And Jorah’s council is that Daario is

00:09:54.370 --> 00:09:59.770
untrustworthy. And Barristan agrees. Even
Dany thinks Daario is treacherous. He might

00:09:59.770 --> 00:10:04.290
fit in to the “three mounts” or “three
betrayals” she is prophesied to suffer.

00:10:04.290 --> 00:10:08.810
But the bigger issue here is that Daario doesn’t make sense as a person. We’re meant to believe

00:10:08.810 --> 00:10:13.760
that Daario is this battle-hardened, self-serving mercenary, who sides with whoever is going

00:10:13.760 --> 00:10:18.890
to win. So why's he sticking with Dany, when
she’s surrounded by enemies and disease,

00:10:18.890 --> 00:10:24.290
and ruin, and other sellswords are abandoning her? Everyone seems to expect Daario to betray

00:10:24.290 --> 00:10:29.450
her, even Dany herself. Like, seriously,
look how many times Dany thinks that Daario

00:10:29.450 --> 00:10:35.920
will betray her. Why doesn’t he? Daario
claims that he loves Dany, but even Dany doesn’t

00:10:35.920 --> 00:10:39.520
believe that – she says Daario’s only
interested in her because she’s a dragon

00:10:39.520 --> 00:10:46.370
queen. Daario wants Daenerys for her power and her dragons. And, well, we do know someone

00:10:46.370 --> 00:10:50.850
else who wants to get into Dany’s pants
for her power and her dragons, don’t we?

00:10:50.850 --> 00:10:54.520
Someone else who is treacherous, dangerous,
gift-giving, sweet-talking, smooth-skinned

00:10:54.520 --> 00:11:01.090
and blue-eyed, of the storm and of the crow.
Euron Greyjoy and Daario Naharis are very

00:11:01.090 --> 00:11:06.050
similar, and being Daario could help Euron,
and the character of Daario doesn’t make

00:11:06.050 --> 00:11:11.790
a lot of sense on his own… Daario=Euron
actually seems pretty believable.

00:11:11.790 --> 00:11:18.500
But let’s address the elephant in the room.
How could all this work? How can Euron and

00:11:18.500 --> 00:11:23.270
Daario be the same person when Daario is in
Slaver’s Bay, and Euron’s half a world

00:11:23.270 --> 00:11:29.090
away, in the Iron Islands? Thing is, Daario
spends most of A Dance with Dragons away from

00:11:29.090 --> 00:11:33.800
Meereen, and we only actually see Euron a
few times, in A Feast for Crows. We don’t

00:11:33.800 --> 00:11:37.910
know exactly how the timings of these two
books line up, but based on the best guesses

00:11:37.910 --> 00:11:42.190
we have, PrivateMajor’s Timeline,
and the Boiled Leather Merged Reading Order,

00:11:42.190 --> 00:11:47.020
we can get a rough idea of how they fit together.
At the start of A Feast for Crows, Euron has

00:11:47.020 --> 00:11:51.090
recently returned to the Iron Islands, and
he stays there until the Kingsmoot in the

00:11:51.090 --> 00:11:56.550
Drowned Man. At this same time, in A Dance
with Dragons, Daario is away on a mission

00:11:56.550 --> 00:12:01.220
to ally with the Lhazarene, and Dany notices
that he’s been away for a worryingly long

00:12:01.220 --> 00:12:06.590
time. By the way, Daario is given gold and
treasure to give the Lhazarene, and at the

00:12:06.590 --> 00:12:11.990
Kingsmoot that follows, Euron gives a bunch
of gold and treasure to the ironborn. Funny

00:12:11.990 --> 00:12:16.880
coincidence, right? So Daario gets back to
Meereen after the Kingsmoot, but he only stays

00:12:16.880 --> 00:12:21.920
long enough to have sex with Dany before he’s
sent away again in the same chapter. We see

00:12:21.920 --> 00:12:26.170
Euron on the Shields a while after that, in
the Reaver, and that’s the last time we

00:12:26.170 --> 00:12:31.550
see Euron. We’re then cryptically told by
Moqorro that Euron is coming for Dany at the

00:12:31.550 --> 00:12:37.470
same time that Daario is sailing to Dany.
So the times do seem to line up, though the

00:12:37.470 --> 00:12:42.580
absences are still kind of a problem – Euron
leaving the Islands after the Kingsmoot seems

00:12:42.580 --> 00:12:47.980
like a very bad idea – shouldn’t he be consolidating
his power? And shouldn’t Daario be leading

00:12:47.980 --> 00:12:53.220
the Stormcrows on their missions? There might
be time for both, but if Euron is Daario,

00:12:53.220 --> 00:12:58.030
he’s a very busy man.
He’s also very bloody quick – it’s a

00:12:58.030 --> 00:13:03.120
long trip from the Iron Islands to Meereen,
and Euron-slash-Daario must have made it like four

00:13:03.120 --> 00:13:08.960
times in one book, albeit a very long book
that is actually two books. There are a bunch

00:13:08.960 --> 00:13:14.210
of reasons why this speed is not a problem.
Firstly, Euron is a pirate King, who’s spent

00:13:14.210 --> 00:13:19.090
years on the sea, sailing all over the world
– if anyone can sail a ship fast, Euron

00:13:19.090 --> 00:13:23.390
Greyjoy can. Especially with the help of
the warlocks and wizards he’s hanging with.

00:13:23.390 --> 00:13:29.150
It’s hinted several times that Euron uses
magic to sail fast. Euron mockingly implies

00:13:29.150 --> 00:13:33.790
that he can “command the winds” and “sail
wherever [he] like[s] and never be becalmed”

00:13:33.790 --> 00:13:38.870
A later passage directly suggests that Euron
controls the winds with blood magic, and

00:13:38.870 --> 00:13:43.620
we know Euron’s ship’s deck is soaked
in blood. There’s evidence that Melisandre’s

00:13:43.620 --> 00:13:48.190
blood magic can command the winds, so why
not Euron’s? It seems likely that Euron

00:13:48.190 --> 00:13:52.880
is using magic to sail fast, and as best we
know, Euron is never in Westeros at

00:13:52.880 --> 00:13:58.370
the same time that Daario is in Meereen. So
it does seem possible that Euron travels between

00:13:58.370 --> 00:14:03.490
Westeros and Slaver’s Bay to play the role
of both the Crow’s Eye and the Stormcrow.

00:14:03.490 --> 00:14:08.150
But there are still are problems. Like, if
Daario is Euron, how does he keep his double

00:14:08.150 --> 00:14:13.700
identity a secret? Euron has a crew of mutes,
but Daario has a company of mercenaries who

00:14:13.700 --> 00:14:18.660
he trusts “as far as [he] can spit”, “Five
hundred sellswords of uncertain loyalty”

00:14:18.660 --> 00:14:22.880
who would notice that their captain keeps
going off on long voyages rather than, y’know,

00:14:22.880 --> 00:14:27.720
doing his job, and leading the company. And
surely someone would notice Euron’s infamous

00:14:27.720 --> 00:14:33.070
ship lurking near Meereen, or reaving for
supplies along the way. However the logistics

00:14:33.070 --> 00:14:38.120
work, there are lots of problems like this,
that make it very hard to believe that Daario=Euron

00:14:38.120 --> 00:14:43.570
could be kept secret.
So… where does this leave us? There are

00:14:43.570 --> 00:14:49.130
lots of little connections and similarities
between Euron and Daario. Being Daario probably

00:14:49.130 --> 00:14:54.110
could fit into Euron’s plan, and it would
explain what Daario’s deal is. It does seem

00:14:54.110 --> 00:14:58.500
possible that Euron could travel the world
fast enough to play both parts, but it’s

00:14:58.500 --> 00:15:04.250
hard to see how he could keep it secret. So
based on what we know, Daario=Euron does seem

00:15:04.250 --> 00:15:09.350
possible. But there’s a simpler explanation
– Daario and Euron are similar because they

00:15:09.350 --> 00:15:15.580
represent similar ideas of violence and self-interest
and their conflict with compassion and honour

00:15:15.580 --> 00:15:20.100
and doing the right thing, which A Song of
Ice and Fire is all about. Every character

00:15:20.100 --> 00:15:24.960
falls somewhere between two extremes. So in
a world with thousands of characters, we

00:15:24.960 --> 00:15:30.350
can’t assume that every suspicious similarity
hides a secret identity. So Euron’s plan

00:15:30.350 --> 00:15:35.230
can still work fine without him being Daario,
and Daario might have his reasons for sticking

00:15:35.230 --> 00:15:39.600
with Dany, maybe he really does love her in
some way, or maybe he’s got something else

00:15:39.600 --> 00:15:46.200
going on that we'll find out about later. So as much as we’d all like to see Daario with an eyepatch bursting out of Yunkish custody

00:15:46.200 --> 00:15:50.970
on the back of Rhaegal, high-fiving Dany on
Drogon as they fly off to spread “fire and

00:15:50.970 --> 00:15:55.790
blood” across Slaver’s Bay, the most reasonable
conclusion is that Daario and Euron are probably

00:15:55.790 --> 00:16:01.610
not the same person. But it’s still fun
to think about.

00:16:01.610 --> 00:16:05.370
